('Food & Drink', 'What is the name of young green wheat that is roasted over fire, rubbed and often cracked, and is used in Egypt as a stuffing for pigeons?', '', 'Bulgur', 'Couscous', 'البرغل', 'الكسكسي'),
('Food & Drink', 'What is the name of the scale, devised by a pharmacist in 1912, that measures how hot chilli peppers are?', '', 'The Brix scale', 'The Mohs scale', 'مقياس بريكس', 'مقياس موس'),
('Food & Drink', 'Which Fatimid caliph of Egypt banned the eating of molokhia in the early 11th century, along with other foods?', '', 'Al-Mu''izz li-Din Allah', 'Al-Mustansir Billah', 'المعز لدين الله', 'المستنصر بالله'),
('Food & Drink', 'The Caesar salad is named after the restaurant owner Caesar Cardini. In which Mexican city was it created, in the 1920s?', '', 'Ensenada', 'Guadalajara', 'إنسينادا', 'غوادالاخارا'),
('Food & Drink', 'Earl Grey tea is flavoured with the oil of which citrus fruit?', '', 'Lemon', 'Grapefruit', 'الليمون', 'الجريب فروت'),
('Food & Drink', 'Which starchy root vegetable do Egyptian Copts traditionally eat at the feast of the Epiphany (Eid El Ghitas), cooked in a green sauce of chard and coriander?', '', 'Sweet potato', 'Turnip', 'البطاطا', 'اللفت');
